git commit -m "feat(explain): add branch detection for default view"
```

## Context

This is Task 3 of ENT-53. We're changing the default `entire explain` behavior from session-centric to branch-centric. The key changes:
1. Show branch name in output
2. Apply default limit of 10 on main/master branches
3. Handle case where no current session exists (show branch info instead of error)

The existing `IsOnDefaultBranch()` function in `git_operations.go` already detects main/master branches.

## Important Notes

- The `runExplainDefault` function signature was updated in Task 2 to accept the new flags
- For this task, focus on branch detection and header output - the full checkpoint listing will come in Task 4
- Don't break existing session explain functionality

